1]Explain indetail about methods in java ?

	->A method is a set of instructions written at one place to perform a particular task is called as method
	->A method can also be called as function or module
	->Every method consists of following 4 things:-
		i)MethodName
		ii)Return type of a method
		iii)Parameters of a method
		iv)Method Body or Method Defination
	->If  a method is not returning anything then the return type should be void
	->If a method returns the value then the return type should be the type of value
	->If a method does not accept any parameters then it should be empty of blank If method accepts parameters 
		then the respective values or variables should be kept inside the parenthesis
	->On the basis of no of parameters and return type of a method thier are 4 types of methods
		
		i]Type-1 method
			->Type-1 method is such a method which will not accept any parameters and it will not return any
			value
			
		ii]Type-2 method
			->Type-2 method is such a method which will accept the parameters but it will not have any return
			type
			
		iii]Type-3 method
			->Type-3 method is such a method which will not accept any parameters but it will return the value
			
		iv]Type-4 method
			->Type-4 method is such a method which will accept parameters and also it will be having the return
			type
			
	->A method can accepts any number of parameters but it will return only one value or list of values
	
Parameters:-
============

	->Parameters are the variables which are present inside the method syntax,to accept the values which are
	passed to the method,they are also known as formal arguments
	
	
Arguments:-
===========

	->Arguments are the variables or values which are passed to the method during method call,they are also
	known as actual arguments.
	
	
